        "original_id": "99f498cd-e5c3-5fbf-9550-891c4dfe74a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vanderbilt University, Bowdoin College, Kentucky Wesleyan College, Methodist Church\n- People: Cornelius Vanderbilt, John Wesley Hughes\n- Places: Brunswick, Maine, Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Millersburg, Kentucky, Owensboro, Kentucky, Nashville, Tennessee, the South\n\nFacts:\n- Bowdoin College was chartered in 1794 when Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Vanderbilt University was founded in 1873.\n- Vanderbilt University was named in honor of Cornelius Vanderbilt.\n- Cornelius Vanderbilt provided Vanderbilt University with its initial $1 million endowment despite never having been to the South.\n- Bowdoin College is a private liberal arts college in Brunswick, Maine.\n- John Wesley Hughes attended Kentucky Wesleyan College in Millersburg, Kentucky, which is now located in Owensboro, Kentucky.\n- John Wesley Hughes served as a pastor in the Kentucky Conference of the Methodist Church before pursuing further education at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tennessee.",
